      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear you—that sense of being worn down to nothing is exhausting, and it makes complete sense that you feel erased. But being \"broken\" isn't a final state; it's a sign that you've endured immense pressure, not that you're worthless. Even if the old you feels gone, what's left is the raw material—still capable of becoming something new, even if it's different from before. You don't have to fix everything today; just let yourself exist as you are right now.",
